## 🚀 Quick Start

### Prerequisites

Make sure you have these installed:

| Tool | Version | Check Command |
|------|---------|---------------|
| Python | 3.10+ | `python --version` |
| Node.js | 18+ | `node --version` |
| npm | 9+ | `npm --version` |
| Git | Latest | `git --version` |

---

### 1️⃣ Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/vishakha2121/autonomous-experiment-planner.git
cd autonomous-experiment-planner
2️⃣ Get Gemini API Key (FREE)
Visit Google AI Studio

Sign in with Google account

Click "Create API Key"

Copy the key (looks like: AIzaSy...)

3️⃣ Backend Setup
bash
# Navigate to backend
cd backend

# Create virtual environment
python -m venv venv

# Activate it
# Windows:
venv\Scripts\activate
# Mac/Linux:
source venv/bin/activate

# Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# Create .env file
copy .env.example .env      # Windows
cp .env.example .env        # Mac/Linux
Edit .env file and add your API key:

env
GEMINI_API_KEY=AIzaSy...your_key_here
DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///./app.db
SECRET_KEY=your_random_secret_key_here
DEBUG=True
Initialize database & run server:

bash
python -m app.db.init_db
uvicorn main:app --reload --port 8000
✅ Backend running at: http://localhost:8000
📚 API Docs at: http://localhost:8000/docs

4️⃣ Frontend Setup
Open a new terminal:

bash
# Navigate to frontend
cd frontend

# Install dependencies
npm install

# Create .env file
copy .env.example .env      # Windows
cp .env.example .env        # Mac/Linux
Edit .env:

env
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8000/api
Start dev server:

bash
npm run dev
✅ Frontend running at: http://localhost:5173

5️⃣ Database Setup (Optional - if using PostgreSQL)
bash
cd database
psql -U postgres -f schema.sql
psql -U postgres -f seed.sql
🔑 Environment Variables
Backend (backend/.env)
Variable	Description	Example
GEMINI_API_KEY	Google Gemini API key	AIzaSy...
DATABASE_URL	Database connection string	sqlite:///./app.db
SECRET_KEY	JWT secret key	random-32-char-string
ALGORITHM	JWT algorithm	HS256
ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRE_MINUTES	Token expiry	1440
DEBUG	Debug mode	True
Frontend (frontend/.env)
Variable	Description	Example
VITE_API_URL	Backend API URL	http://localhost:8000/api
📸 Screenshots
🏠 Dashboard
https://docs/screenshots/dashboard.png
Real-time analytics and experiment overview

🧬 Protocol Generation
https://docs/screenshots/protocol.png
AI-generated experimental protocol with steps

🕸️ Knowledge Graph
https://docs/screenshots/knowledge-graph.png
Interactive graph of scientific entities

🎯 Bayesian Optimization
https://docs/screenshots/optimization.png
Parameter optimization with convergence chart

🤖 AI Assistant
https://docs/screenshots/assistant.png
Chat with AI about your experiments

🧪 How It Works
Workflow
text
1. User creates experiment
        ↓
2. AI generates protocol (Gemini)
        ↓
3. Knowledge Graph finds related concepts
        ↓
4. Bayesian Optimizer suggests parameters
        ↓
5. LLM predicts outcomes
        ↓
6. System recommends follow-up experiments
Example Use Case
Input:

"Design an experiment to test the effect of temperature on enzyme activity"

System Output:

✅ Protocol: 8-step procedure with materials, safety notes, timeline

✅ Parameters: Optimal temperature range (30-45°C) via Bayesian opt

✅ Prediction: Peak activity at 37°C, denaturation above 60°C (87% confidence)

✅ Follow-ups: Test pH interaction, substrate concentration effects

✅ Knowledge Graph: Links to enzyme kinetics, Michaelis-Menten, related papers

🧪 Running Tests
Backend Tests
bash
cd backend
pytest -v
pytest --cov=app tests/
Frontend Tests
bash
cd frontend
npm test
📚 API Documentation
Once backend is running, visit:

Swagger UI: http://localhost:8000/docs

ReDoc: http://localhost:8000/redoc

Key Endpoints
Method	Endpoint	Description
POST	/api/auth/register	Register new user
POST	/api/auth/login	Login & get token
GET	/api/experiments	List all experiments
POST	/api/experiments	Create experiment
POST	/api/protocols/generate	Generate protocol
POST	/api/predictions/predict	Predict outcomes
POST	/api/optimization/run	Run Bayesian opt
GET	/api/knowledge-graph	Get graph data
GET	/api/recommendations	Get follow-ups
