🧪 How It Works
Workflow
text
1. User creates experiment
        ↓
2. AI generates protocol (Gemini)
        ↓
3. Knowledge Graph finds related concepts
        ↓
4. Bayesian Optimizer suggests parameters
        ↓
5. LLM predicts outcomes
        ↓
6. System recommends follow-up experiments
Example Use Case
Input:

"Design an experiment to test the effect of temperature on enzyme activity"

System Output:

✅ Protocol: 8-step procedure with materials, safety notes, timeline

✅ Parameters: Optimal temperature range (30-45°C) via Bayesian opt

✅ Prediction: Peak activity at 37°C, denaturation above 60°C (87% confidence)

✅ Follow-ups: Test pH interaction, substrate concentration effects

✅ Knowledge Graph: Links to enzyme kinetics, Michaelis-Menten, related papers

🧪 Running Tests
Backend Tests
bash
cd backend
pytest -v
pytest --cov=app tests/
Frontend Tests
bash
cd frontend
npm test
📚 API Documentation
Once backend is running, visit:

Swagger UI: http://localhost:8000/docs

ReDoc: http://localhost:8000/redoc

Key Endpoints
Method	Endpoint	Description
POST	/api/auth/register	Register new user
POST	/api/auth/login	Login & get token
GET	/api/experiments	List all experiments
POST	/api/experiments	Create experiment
POST	/api/protocols/generate	Generate protocol
POST	/api/predictions/predict	Predict outcomes
POST	/api/optimization/run	Run Bayesian opt
GET	/api/knowledge-graph	Get graph data
GET	/api/recommendations	Get follow-ups
